{
  "summary": "Replaces the node's `-privatebroadcast` implementation with isolated, stateless broadcast jobs managed under a new `src/privbcast` module. With `-privatebroadcast` enabled, `sendrawtransaction` queues a background job on a dedicated thread that performs DNS seed discovery and BIP324 announcements strictly through a Tor SOCKS5 proxy using fresh isolation credentials and a pre-drawn schedule. All legacy private broadcast connection types, queue logic, and bypass rules are deleted from `CConnman` and `PeerManager`, and new `getprivatebroadcastinfo` and `abortprivatebroadcast` RPCs are added.",
  "problem": "The prior private broadcast implementation was directly coupled to node networking state in `CConnman` and `PeerManager`. This shared state risked privacy leaks via recipient interactions, node mempool feedback, or adversarial inputs crashing the node, while adding substantial special-casing to core P2P handling.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes the isolated architecture protects 'against IP address linkage and not crashing the node on adversarial inputs (which is a leak in itself)'",
    "Commit messages and design docs specify strict invariants ensuring 'Nothing a recipient does, and nothing the node sees of the transaction coming back, changes the plan, and the transaction enters the node's mempool only when it returns from the network.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#36608"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "A large architectural rewrite (+6078/-3044 across 78 files) that introduces an independent byte-driven SOCKS5 client and BIP324 attempt state machine in `src/privbcast`, while deleting legacy private broadcast code and tests from `net.cpp` and `net_processing.cpp`.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Initial description was generated without the patch diff (patch-id nopatch); no structural changes to the PR.",
  "card": "Replaces Bitcoin Core's private broadcast subsystem with isolated, stateless jobs running on dedicated worker threads. When -privatebroadcast is set, sendrawtransaction delegates to an event-driven job that discovers seeds and announces transactions over BIP324 exclusively via Tor using isolated proxy credentials and a fixed schedule, entering the local mempool only after being echoed back from the network. This eliminates privacy leakage vectors and removes extensive special-case logic previously embedded inside CConnman and PeerManager. Unblocks follow-up package relay support for private broadcasts in #36608.",
